mple or averaging models.","Revenue per day trend: +2.54% per year, NOT statistically significant (p = 0.142).","Best model on backtest WAPE: Random Forest at 1.78% WAPE; Naive benchmark 2.37%; runner-up Calendar-adjusted Naive at 1.92% (margin 0.14 points).","The margin is below 0.5 points, so the top models are effectively tied.","Planning model: Calendar-adjusted Naive (1.92% WAPE), because it is the simplest model whose backtest WAPE is within 0.5 points of the best; simpler models are easier to explain and less likely to over-fit.","Planning-model forecast: 2022-01: 160,396 units (95% range 152,520 to 168,272); 2022-02: 144,874 units (95% range 134,814 to 154,934); 2022-03: 160,396 units (95% range 146,755 to 174,037); total 465,666 units.","Planning-model test bias: +0.09%, meaning almost unbiased.","Random Forest and XGBoost trained on only 9 rows, too few to learn reliable patterns.","Largest regions by recent share: Saarland 6.7%, Hessen 6.5%, Hamburg 6.4%."]},"fallback":{"seasonality_trend":"There is no meaningful volume trend: 2.32% per year with p = 0.212, which is not statistically significant. Each calendar month has been observed only once, so a seasonal pattern cannot be separated from random noise (needs 24+ months). The number of days in a month explains R² = 0.76 of the month-to-month variation, so calendar-aware models capture the main systematic pattern.","best_model":"Random Forest performed best on backtest WAPE at 1.78% (single test window: MAPE 1.56%, WAPE 1.60%). It beats the Naive benchmark (2.37%) by 0.59 percentage points. However, its margin over the runner-up, Calendar-adjusted Naive (1.92%), is only 0.14 percentage points, which is within the noise of this small sample, so the top models should be treated as equally good. For planning we therefore recommend Calendar-adjusted Naive (1.92%), the simplest model within 0.5 points of the best: it is easier to explain and less likely to over-fit. The machine-learning models trained on only 9 rows, too few to learn reliable patterns.","recommendations":["Plan production from 2022-01 to 2022-03 at about 465,666 units in total using Calendar-adjusted Naive (95% range for 2022-01: 152,520 to 168,272).","Forecast bias on the test window is small (0.09%), so production can follow the forecast without a systematic correction.","Use the days in each month when setting monthly production targets: shorter months such as February need proportionally less volume.","Allocate distribution by regional share: Saarland is the largest market at 6.7% of recent volume (about 31,109 units over the forecast horizon).","Stay with simple, calendar-aware models until two full years of sales exist, then re-test for seasonality before adding complexity.","Re-run the forecast as each new month of actual sales arrives and switch models only if a more complex one consistently beats the simple benchmark in the backtest."],"limitations":["The dataset is synthetic (simulated sales), so patterns reflect the simulator, not real consumers.","Only 12 months of history: seasonality cannot be tested and machine-learning models have very few training rows.","The test window is 3 months, so one unusual month can move MAPE noticeably."],"confidence":"medium","source":"rule-based"}}